# Phase 3: WebRTC / Video Call Integration

This phase integrates real-time video/audio calling between Customers and Professionals using **Agora** for media routing and **Firestore** for call signaling (bypassing the old Node.js socket server for signaling since we've migrated the database to Firebase).

## Goal Description
Connect the Customer and Expert apps through a seamless calling experience. When a customer initiates a call, the expert receives an incoming call notification in real-time. Upon acceptance, both parties join an Agora video/audio channel.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Firestore Call Signaling
Since we moved users and experts to Firestore, we will use a new `calls` collection in Firestore to handle signaling instead of Socket.io.
- **Start Call:** Customer creates a `calls` document with `status: 'ringing'`.
- **Ringing:** Professional app listens for `calls` documents where `expertId == myId` and `status == 'ringing'` to show the incoming call popup.
- **Accept/Reject:** Professional updates the document status to `accepted` or `rejected`.
- **Join:** Customer listens to the document. When `status` changes to `accepted`, both join the Agora channel.

### 2. Agora Token Generation
We will continue to use the existing Node.js backend **only** for generating secure Agora tokens (`/calls/token` endpoint), as this requires the secure App Certificate which cannot be exposed on the frontend.

### 3. Live Billing & End Call
We will implement a basic Firestore-based billing update at the end of the call.
- When the call ends, calculate the duration.
- Deduct the calculated amount from the Customer's `walletBalance` in Firestore.
- Add the calculated amount to the Expert's `walletBalance` in Firestore.
- Update the call document status to `ended`.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **User Review Required:**
> We are using Firestore for signaling instead of the old Socket.io server to keep the architecture unified with Phase 1 and 2. The Agora tokens will still be generated by the Node backend. Is this approach acceptable to you?

## Verification Plan
1. **Automated Tests:** Verify that the code compiles successfully across Customer and Professional apps.
2. **Manual Verification:**
   - Log into a Customer account and an Expert account on separate devices (or separate Chrome windows).
   - Initiate a call from the Customer app.
   - Verify the Expert app receives the incoming call modal.
   - Accept the call and verify both apps join the Agora room successfully and can communicate.
   - End the call and verify wallet balances are updated in Firestore.
